ance and trade. For the visitor, there is a seemingly endless choice of historical sites, shopping, museums, food, art galleries, nightlife, and activities.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"London","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/London","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"London is the largest city in the United Kingdom, spread along the Thames in the south of England. The Tower of London, Westminster Abbey and the British Museum lead a long list, and the main sights run to seventeen hours. June to September is best.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":8961989,"visit_h":16.8}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-british-museum","name":"British Museum","kind":"Museum","lat":51.51944,"lon":-0.12694,"dist_km":1.3,"rank_score":11.73,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-westminster-abbey","name":"Westminster Abbey","kind":"Cathedral","lat":51.4994,"lon":-0.12737,"dist_km":0.9,"rank_score":11.45,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-tower-of-london","name":"Tower of London","kind":"Museum","lat":51.5082,"lon":-0.0762,"dist_km":3.5,"rank_score":11.39,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-big-ben","name":"Big Ben","kind":"Tower","lat":51.50067,"lon":-0.12457,"dist_km":0.8,"rank_score":11.39,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-tower-bridge","name":"Tower Bridge","kind":"Bridge","lat":51.50556,"lon":-0.07528,"dist_km":3.6,"rank_score":11.35,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-london-bridge","name":"London Bridge","kind":"Bridge","lat":51.50806,"lon":-0.08778,"dist_km":2.7,"rank_score":11.19,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-british-library","name":"British Library","kind":"Landmark","lat":51.52944,"lon":-0.12694,"dist_km":2.4,"rank_score":11.19,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-st-paul-s-cathedral","name":"St Paul's Cathedral","kind":"Cathedral","lat":51.51378,"lon":-0.09831,"dist_km":2.1,"rank_score":11.11,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/St_Pauls_aerial_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-St_Pauls